@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-fixtures`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`
IMPORT `ito66-c-credit-points`

-- ===========================================================================
-- THE ISRAEL TAX AUTHORITY'S OWN TABLES, as tests.
--
-- An independent reading of the same text by the regulator, published as
-- employer circulars.  An aid, not a source of law: where the circular and
-- the deposited text disagreed, the text would govern and the disagreement
-- would be a finding.  Neither circular was read before the rules were
-- written; they were fetched to date the text (ito66-tax-years.l4).
--
--  * ITA circular 2024-000012, 3 January 2024, "חוק הגדלת נקודות זיכוי להורים
--    במס הכנסה, התשפ״ג–2023".  Para 3.1 (the married woman), 3.2 (the married
--    man), column "מ-2024":
--        age in the tax year 6-12 : woman 2, man 1
--        age in the tax year 13-17: woman 2, man 1
--  * ITA circular 2024-001090, 26 March 2024, "חוק סיוע להורים לילדים עד גיל
--    שלוש (תיקוני חקיקה), התשפ״ד-2024".  Para 3, "נקודות הזיכוי ... לכל הורה",
--    column "משנת 2024":
--        שנת לידה 2.5 ; 1: 4.5 ; 2: 4.5 ; 3: 3.5
--    and "האישה רשאית להעביר נקודת זיכוי אחת מתוך 2.5 נקודות הזיכוי להן היא
--    זכאית בשנת הלידה, לשנה שלאחר שנת הלידה."
--
-- URLs, retrieval and sha256 are in NOTES.md section 7.  Both circulars also
-- print the figures "עד שנת 2023" (1.5 / 2.5 / 2.5 / 2.5, and 1 / 0 for ages
-- 13-17); the deposited text is not the law for 2023, so the last tests
-- check that the encoding REFUSES 2023 rather than answering it with the
-- 2024 figures.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — the Israel Tax Authority's tables for 2024 onward`

-- A married couple in a tax year, the woman claiming a separate calculation,
-- with one child of both born in the given tax year.
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `born`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`a married couple in tax year` `the year` `with one child born in` `born` MEANS
    `spouses in tax year` `the year`
        `; registered` (`a salaried spouse:` `a man`   `earning` 200000 `; claims under (a)` FALSE)
        `; other`      (`a salaried spouse:` `a woman` `earning` 120000 `; claims under (a)` TRUE)
        `; children` (LIST `a child of both, born in tax year` `born`)
        `; common source` NOTHING

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `born`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the woman's points in tax year` `the year` `for a child born in` `born` MEANS
    `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`a married couple in tax year` `the year` `with one child born in` `born`) `for` (`a child of both, born in tax year` `born`)

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
      `born`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the man's points in tax year` `the year` `for a child born in` `born` MEANS
    `s 66(c)(4)-(6) — the credit points of the` `registered spouse` `in` (`a married couple in tax year` `the year` `with one child born in` `born`) `for` (`a child of both, born in tax year` `born`)

-- 2024-001090 para 3, "לכל הורה", from 2024: the woman.
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2024 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2023 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2022 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2021 EQUALS 3.5
-- ... and the man.
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2024 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2023 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2022 EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2021 EQUALS 3.5

-- 2024-000012 paras 3.1 and 3.2, from 2024, at both ends of each age band.
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2018 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2012 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2011 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the woman's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2007 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2018 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2012 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2011 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the man's points in tax year` 2024 `for a child born in` 2007 EQUALS 1

-- The same rows in 2025, through the whole of s 66(c) for the couple: the
-- woman has ½ under s 36A beside the children's points.
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`a married couple in tax year` 2025 `with one child born in` 2025) EQUALS `in a separate calculation` (`Credit points under section 66(c)` 0.5 0 2.5)
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `registered spouse` `in` (`a married couple in tax year` 2025 `with one child born in` 2024) EQUALS `in a separate calculation` (`Credit points under section 66(c)` 0 0 4.5)
#ASSERT `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `registered spouse` `in` (`a married couple in tax year` 2025 `with one child born in` 2010) EQUALS `in a separate calculation` (`Credit points under section 66(c)` 0 0 1)

-- 2024-001090: the woman may move one of the 2.5 birth-year points to the next year.
`a child born 2024, the mother moving a point` MEANS
    `a child born in tax year` 2024 `; of the registered spouse` TRUE `; of the other spouse` TRUE `; mother defers a point` TRUE `; interest` 0
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `a child born 2024, the mother moving a point` `in tax year` 2024 EQUALS 1.5
#ASSERT `s 66(c)(4)(a)-(a1) — the mother's credit points for` `a child born 2024, the mother moving a point` `in tax year` 2025 EQUALS 5.5

-- "עד שנת 2023": not this text.  The encoding must decline, not answer 2.5 or 2.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `spouse who is not the registered spouse` `in` (`a married couple in tax year` 2023 `with one child born in` 2023)
        BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` `registered spouse` `in` (`a married couple in tax year` 2023 `with one child born in` 2010)
        BECAUSE "this encoding does not hold the text of section 66 for a tax year before 2024"
